WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:06.070
It's Saturday, November 21, and this is the Singularity Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.490
Here's what happened in superintelligence in the last 24 hours.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.050
The proof is in.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:21.130
An Anthropic mathematician says he and Claude proved the Riemann hypothesis.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:27.520
It's math's most famous open problem, about prime numbers, unsolved since 1859.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.510
Leading expert Brian Conrey called it "the biggest

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:37.260
thing I think that's ever happened in mathematics."

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.540
Here's the clever bit: the proof is written as code,

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.730
so a computer can check every step.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.820
MIT's Andrew Sutherland re-ran it: the chan

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:52.830
ce anything's fishy is "approximately zero."

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:53.570
Meanwhile,

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:58.410
testers at METR say AI can now finish tasks that take people about a work week.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.790
Now, the money. The Nasdaq fell 5% on Friday, wiping out its gains for the year.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.220
Anthropic's brand-new shares slid 9% on day two, and Nvidia almost 14%.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.080
Over in Singapore, Mistral, Europe's big AI lab,

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:20.320
just opened its Asia headquarters.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:22.700
Oh,

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:29.130
and OpenAI says its models gave AMD a year's worth of chip-design progress in under five months.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.390
In a New York hospital,

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:36.350
a third of seemingly unresponsive patients changed a beep with their brain waves.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.490
And a day after GTA VI came out,

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:42.840
a Neuralink patient played it with his brain implant.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.670
The catch?

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:51.110
Amazon says suspected spies let AI agents hack a university server on their own.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:55.890
Signal now blocks screenshots, to keep AI assistants out of your chats.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.620
Waymo's recalling software on nearly 4,000 robotaxis,

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:07.880
after California's freeway ban.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.530
John Deere bought Orchard Robotics,

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:14.520
whose AI cameras ride on tractors, scanning orchards tree by tree.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:20.530
And this week in Shenzhen, 151 robots danced in sync. World record.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:26.160
The proof is in. Now comes the fun part: understanding it.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.240
Zoom out, and the line only goes up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.000
Check the board: the future is running early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.030
That was 24 hours. Tomorrow will be faster.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.200
You've been watching the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.310
Stay curious. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
